          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for a principal, then the Malayalam for tuition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: വാദിക്കുക",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വാദിക്കുക — vādikkuka — \"to plead a case; to argue\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അവൾ പുതിയ നിയമത്തിന് എതിരെ വാദിച്ചു. avaḷ putiya niyamattinŭ etire vādiccu. She argued against the new law."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past: വാദിച്ചു, vādiccu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "For a cause: -ക്ക് വേണ്ടി വാദിക്കുക (vādikkuka); against it: -ന് എതിരെ വാദിക്കുക (vādikkuka)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വാദിക്കുക (vādikkuka) is built from Sanskrit vāda, \"speech\" (CDIAL 11507), from the root vad, \"to speak\", with the Malayalam verb ending -ിക്കുക. To argue is to keep speaking for one side."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
