          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "യുക്തി — yukti — \"logic; reasoning\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അവന്റെ വാദത്തിൽ ഒരു യുക്തിയും ഇല്ല. avanṟe vādattil oru yuktiyuṁ illa. There is no logic at all in his argument."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A bookish word for good sense in an argument."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "യുക്തി (yukti) is borrowed from Sanskrit yukti, first \"union, joining\" and \"application\", and later \"reasoning, argument\" (CDIAL 10480; Monier-Williams). It comes from the root yuj, \"to join\", the root of യോജിക്കുക: reasoning joins one thought to the next."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
