              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വസ്തുത (vastuta) is built on Sanskrit vastu, \"a thing that exists; an affair\" (CDIAL 11449), with the abstract ending -ത; Sanskrit itself has vastutā (Monier-Williams). A fact is what a thing really is."
            }
