          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നിഗമനം — nigamanaṁ — \"a conclusion\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "എല്ലാം കേട്ട ശേഷം അവർ ഒരു നിഗമനത്തിൽ എത്തി. ellāṁ kēṭṭa śēṣaṁ avar oru nigamanattil etti. After hearing everything, they reached a conclusion."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "To reach a conclusion is നിഗമനത്തിൽ എത്തുക."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നിഗമനം (nigamanaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit nigamana, which in the old books of logic names the summing up of an argument, its conclusion (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
